{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1092231-lunar-rage","id":1092231,"title":"Lunar Rage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-13T22:04:28-07:00","id":1092231,"title":"Lunar Rage","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted, Third Edition, page 46</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Broken Bonds</b><br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted were created to be the Solars\u2019 seconds, their spouses, and the sacred guardians of the Old Realm. The bond defined the Lunars; it sang within their very Essence.<br /> <br /> So too did the bond\u2019s destruction. The Old Realm fell; the Solars were murdered, their spirits banished beyond Lunar ken. The Lunars changed. They\u2019re still changing. A deep rage lives in their Essence, and a deep wound. Their sleep is tormented by visions of loss, of murder, of the past. The Lunars are compelled to shatter the chains binding them to the past\u2014to tear down the stolen remnants of the First Age, to raze the Sidereal and Terrestrial hegemony that dares to wear the ancient name of the Realm. The Silver Pact exists to facilitate this.<br /> <br /> Some Lunars resist the primal howl that shivers in their Essence. They harness their rage to fight for that which they cherish, or bend their powerful instincts to their own benefit as they walk another road. There is tension between these Lunars and the Silver Pact traditionalists, but also common bonds; the two trade favors and mark debts more often than they shed one another\u2019s blood.<br /> <br /> The return of the Solars changes everything for Luna\u2019s Chosen. Neither Lunar camp seeks to turn back the clock, nor wishes to return to defining themselves as the shadows cast by the Chosen of the sun. Something stirs in the Lunars\u2019 hearts, but none can yet say what it is or what it means.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted, Third Edition, page 46</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By unleashing the rage deep inside, Lunars may evoke monstrous battle-forms.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted, Third Edition, page 47</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Play one of the Lunar Exalted if you want... to be the inheritor of an ancient vendetta, empowered by rage to be nearly unstoppable.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted, Third Edition, page 106</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...each Lunar Exaltation brings with it a hungry turmoil of the soul.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1070320#post1070320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am intrigued by the mention of Rage in the Essence of the Lunars in their blurb in the core. Especially under the Broken Bonds header, it gives an intriguing and excitingly distinct view of their relationship with the First Age, the Age of Sorrows and their opposition to the Realm. It also brings something else to mind...<br /> <br /> Will Lunars still use Limit in this Edition, or will they have a new thing to track, a la Resonance or Paradox? If they are still using Limit, will their experience of it be distinct from Solars, and will it involve this Rage in their Essence at all?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1070341#post1070341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Limit isn't something we've gotten around to discussing fully. I can say that I don't want to tie the Lunar's rage entirely to Limit, something that many players perceive as a drawback or ignore altogether. Rage something they drawn on with their Charms, one of the sources of their power. They're predators, but they aren't driven by hunger\u2014rather, it's their rage that sustains their will to hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>What does this tell us?</b><br /> <br /> 1) Lunar Rage seems akin to Sidereal Arcane Fate. Breaking the Constellation of the Mask afflicted Sidereals with the mixed curse of Arcane Fate, and breaking of the Solar Bonds afflicted the Lunar Exalted with Rage.<br /> <br /> 2) Lunar Rage is something distinct from their Great Curse. Comparatively, it is a new problem<br /> <br /> 3) It is also <i>a new source of strength</i>. I remember Holden once writing a short story in which Chejop Kejak is getting stitched back together by a god of medicine after an encounter with a Lunar, and the Sidereal is talking about how he predicted that the Lunar Exalted would become the monsters he painted them to be, and lamenting that they <i>exceeded his expectations</i>.<br /> <br /> 4) The wounds left by the broken Solar Bonds, and the resulting Rage, have not only changed the Essence of the Lunar Exalted permanently, but the potential depths of the changes haven't yet been fully explored. The Lunar Exalted might experiment with their altered nature, and perhaps find a way to change even more.<br /> <br /> 5) Vance declined to comment on whether Rage would be represented with points, like Sidereal Paradox or the Rage points of the Classical World of Darkness' Garou werewolves. So, that possibility is still on the table.<br /> <br /> 6) This Rage is not something that the Lunar Exalted choose; rather, they are unavoidably angry, and every one of them has to decide how to deal with that. Many of them choose to harness that anger towards personal ends which have nothing to do with the injustices suffered by their previous incarnations.<br /> <br /> 7) Few Lunars welcome the idea of fixing the Solar Bonds that proved so disastrously unreliable and painful. Why invite that same heartache again?<br /> <br /> 8) The language surrounding Rage leaves little doubt about its intended emotional tenor. &quot;Broken, wound, torment, loss, shatter, tear, raze, howl, shiver, vendetta, hungry turmoil&quot;... Lunar Rage stems from pain. Lunar Rage is angry and violent. It's not &quot;passion&quot; or &quot;obsession&quot; or &quot;focus&quot;, it's pain and the anger that comes from being hurt. Insofar as it resembles hunger, it is starvation to the point of torture.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>What does this NOT tell us?</b><br /> <br /> 1) It does NOT tell us that every Lunar Exalted is always seeing red, all of the time.<br /> <br /> 2) It does NOT tell us that the Lunar Exalted have no control over their Rage at all. Indeed, it explicitly tells us that Lunars find it possible to harness that anger towards their own purposes, and seems to imply that a Lunar can disassociate themselves from that Rage -- seeing it as something imposed upon them rather than rightfully belonging to them.<br /> <br /> 3) It does NOT tell us that Rage is the only source of Lunar power. On the first page of the Ask The Devs thread, Robert Vance waxed lyrical about the themes of Hunting, Predation, and Symbiosis. Also, shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> 4) It does NOT tell us that any Lunar has found a way to Chill Out. Maybe they can appease or simply exhaust the Rage (especially if it is represented with points), but it apparently never really goes away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-14-2017, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T22:26:44-07:00","id":1092237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted, Third Edition, page 46</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...they remain caught on the fangs of the past, and until they escape it, they cannot truly claim the freedom Luna has promised them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage is the antithesis of freedom.<br /> <br /> Freedom comes in many forms, and one of the most important is your state of mind. A home becomes a prison when you are placed under house arrest, and a prison can become a home if you have no desire to leave. Being given too many options can paralyze someone with indecision, whereas being restricted by rules can free someone to explore the remaining possibilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> When someone detains you against your will, you can respond with anger, and use that anger to smash away the barrier that restricts your physical freedom to leave. When someone blackmails you, you can respond with anger, and use that anger to fuel you to out-scheme your nemesis.<br /> <br /> But in choosing to be angry, you choose to make your freedom conditional. You choose to care so much about something that you cannot feel free without it. In a sense, you enslave yourself to this thing.<br /> <br /> Further, if your rage proves insufficient to secure the condition you've placed on your freedom, then you still lack your conditional freedom while also being enslaved to rage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, it's good that the Lunar Exalted do not find simply giving up to be any more natural to accomplish than other human beings. It's hard!<br /> <br /> What's more, the logical extreme of this approach isn't healthy, either, as a life is not worth living if you refuse to care about anything enough to live for it. This sort of hollowness is what the soulless Raksha have to carefully balance, and what makes mortals vulnerable to that controversial Charm, Cup Boils Over.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, it remains ironic that the Exalted most capable of simply avoiding, escaping, and hiding from trouble are the ones most motivated to stay and fight.<br /> <br /> But it also makes a lot of sense, because if the Lunar Exalted didn't have a strong motivation to fight, they would be rather boring. They'd largely just run away and hide from the Realm and Sidereals.<br /> <br /> If they spent all of their time hiding in the Threshold and Wyld and cutting away every passion that might tie them down, they would be indistinguishable from the Raksha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-14-2017, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T06:17:38-07:00","id":1092317,"title":"","content":"I disagree. There is nothing so liberating or terrifying than rage. Rage allows you to circumvent your fears, to ignore social convictions, and to do great (and terrible) things that society tells you are impossible (or unwise).<br /> <br /> The Rage of the Lunar Exalted was probably made manifest as a narrative structure in their Exaltation when they fled to the Wyld without proper protections. Their tattoos protect them from the Wyld by using the narrative of their Rage to protect them from the narrative of the Wyld. Rage could possibly also have other uses.<br /> <br /> I see Rage as a separate track that mimics Limit, but is separate from Limit. With each point of Rage, the Lunar gains a bonus attribute dot until the Lunar gains enough Rage to enter into a Rage frenzy for a scene, after which Rage become 0 again. While it Rage frenzy, I imagine that the Lunar enters DBT and gains bonuses based on their amount of Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T06:44:20-07:00","id":1092321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1092231-lunar-rage?p=1092317#post1092317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. There is nothing so liberating or terrifying than rage. Rage allows you to circumvent your fears, to ignore social convictions, and to do great (and terrible) things that society tells you are impossible (or unwise).</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong, but that's not the whole truth about rage.<br /> <br /> Freedom and captivity are almost two sides of the same coin, as I think my post above should have made clear. One man's freedom is another man's captivity; the thing that makes you free, taken too far, can take you captive, and trying to become too free leaves you a captive to ennui.<br /> <br /> I started with a bold and controversial claim in order to grab your attention, but please don't simply ignore everything I say after that point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Rage of the Lunar Exalted was probably made manifest as a narrative structure in their Exaltation when they fled to the Wyld without proper protections. Their tattoos protect them from the Wyld by using the narrative of their Rage to protect them from the narrative of the Wyld. </div> </div> </div>The problem with this opinion is that NOTHING in the official text supports it. The official text tells us that Rage comes from the broken Solar Bonds.<br /> <br /> FURTHER, other texts and developer comments repeatedly make it clear that the Lunar Exalted didn't lose their Castes or their stability to the Wyld, this time. They broke their own Castes, and Chimerism is a choice rather than a disease.<br /> <br /> Third Edition is working hard to give agency back to the Lunar Exalted instead of the Wyld, so I doubt they're going to turn around and start letting the Wyld bully the Lunar Exalted AGAIN.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see Rage as a separate track that mimics Limit, but is separate from Limit. With each point of Rage, the Lunar gains a bonus attribute dot until the Lunar gains enough Rage to enter into a Rage frenzy for a scene, after which Rage become 0 again. While it Rage frenzy, I imagine that the Lunar enters DBT and gains bonuses based on their amount of Rage. </div> </div> </div>That sounds too much like Limit. Remember, Vance wants to make Rage sufficiently separate and different from Limit and Limit Breaking because he knows that some people leave those things out of the game.<br /> <br /> Apparently, he feels that Rage is too important to the Lunar play experience to be left on the cutting room floor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T09:05:09-07:00","id":1092345,"title":"","content":"The analogy between Lunar rage and Sidereal Arcane Fate is imperfect, because Arcane Fate is a drawback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T09:15:05-07:00","id":1092348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1092231-lunar-rage?p=1092345#post1092345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The analogy between Lunar rage and Sidereal Arcane Fate is imperfect, because Arcane Fate is a drawback.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat! Thanks for the hint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T17:58:59-07:00","id":1092593,"title":"","content":"A useful application of Lunar Rage would be sharing it with other people.<br /> <br /> Solar Exalted separate effects like Fury-Inciting Speech and Route-Stemming Gesture into different Abilities, but for Lunar Exalted the Charisma Charm tree could easily have something similar to both effects. The power to turn a crowd into a mob, and a mob into a howling war-band.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T07:31:24-07:00","id":1095123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1092231-lunar-rage?p=1092237#post1092237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rage is the antithesis of freedom.<br /> <br /> Freedom comes in many forms, and one of the most important is your state of mind. A home becomes a prison when you are placed under house arrest, and a prison can become a home if you have no desire to leave. Being given too many options can paralyze someone with indecision, whereas being restricted by rules can free someone to explore the remaining possibilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> When someone detains you against your will, you can respond with anger, and use that anger to smash away the barrier that restricts your physical freedom to leave. When someone blackmails you, you can respond with anger, and use that anger to fuel you to out-scheme your nemesis.<br /> <br /> But in choosing to be angry, you choose to make your freedom conditional. You choose to care so much about something that you cannot feel free without it. In a sense, you enslave yourself to this thing.<br /> <br /> Further, if your rage proves insufficient to secure the condition you've placed on your freedom, then you still lack your conditional freedom while also being enslaved to rage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, it's good that the Lunar Exalted do not find simply giving up to be any more natural to accomplish than other human beings. It's hard!<br /> <br /> What's more, the logical extreme of this approach isn't healthy, either, as a life is not worth living if you refuse to care about anything enough to live for it. This sort of hollowness is what the soulless Raksha have to carefully balance, and what makes mortals vulnerable to that controversial Charm, Cup Boils Over.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, it remains ironic that the Exalted most capable of simply avoiding, escaping, and hiding from trouble are the ones most motivated to stay and fight.<br /> <br /> But it also makes a lot of sense, because if the Lunar Exalted didn't have a strong motivation to fight, they would be rather boring. They'd largely just run away and hide from the Realm and Sidereals.<br /> <br /> If they spent all of their time hiding in the Threshold and Wyld and cutting away every passion that might tie them down, they would be indistinguishable from the Raksha.</div> </div> </div> </div>That bit about being able to escape and become anyone or do anything without concern for the struggle, I think it's arguably why shapeshifters are more often antagonistic or dangerous as opposed to straight up Heroes<br /> <br /> Not everywhere of course, Zeus is a shapeshifter and everyone I think knows about Maui now<br /> <br /> But more with our culture and our tradition shapeshifting is scary. it is effectively deception at its most basic. it's why the devil being a shape-shifter or hidden in plain sight or the ultimate in deception is his biggest weapon.<br /> Or was for the longest time until he became the sort of the god of secular superiority or something in romantic interpretation<br /> <br /> Even ignoring the werewolf the apocalypse baggage this is probably the hardest part about Lunar design. Shapeshifters tend to be lone figures or monsters at the edges. There's one of them in a story if there's more than one it generally tends to be a massive chase or a bunch of Chaos<br /> <br /> So if you have an entire race of shapeshifters, or all about shape-shifting, you have to come up with more and more and more limits on how they can be. So they are people whose actions matter and have an investment in the ongoing struggles and setting.<br /> So you make it they can't disguise themselves perfectly with tells<br /> You make them damaged or have a history where they absolutely have to do something<br /> You make them predatious so at the very least someone in the setting has been affected by their activities<br /> and humans being what we are means we'll get caught up in some petty b******* when we really could just give up and enjoy life<br /> <br /> It's why in superhero comics often shape-shifting and disguise is the province of villains. Superheroes do shapeshift or use disguises but try not to make a habit of it or even if they do it's usually a sign pointing to a sort of moral ambiguity or grayness<br /> <br /> Or it becomes a moral point to condemn or question them on.<br /> Superman's Behavior to the family of the Daily Planet, portection or trolling<br /> Who is real Bruce Wayne or Batman<br /> <br /> The problem is when you possess the ultimate tool of Escape- well -it's like the world is your internet anon board.<br /> that's a powerful privilege. This isn't to say that change in and of itself can't be tolerated or be a crucial aspect of a hero or even easy to write<br /> <br /> But the ability to literally change who you are in the eyes of others and what you can do in terms of your ability and needs to the world and the life you can lead but may leave with effectively a snap of your fingers<br /> Even if that ability cost you the life of another to gain...<br /> Well after you make enough Bank what's to stop you?<br /> <br /> This means despite the fact that their experiences should give way to a very diverse and unique cast of people<br /> The lunars have to be relatively generic and homogeneous<br /> If yoiu put all the colors together in paint you end up with an indistinct sludge and with light you end up with white or clear with no unique aspects<br /> <br /> Uniformity<br /> Indistinction<br /> crap or generic.<br /> <br /> Unless the ability to do this is literally the entire focus of the game, which is why I think the fair folk ended up being able to do the shapeshifting predator and trickster and other thing so better. Their entire approach with the setting is that they are hostile, alien, and divorced but with it<br /> Ultimately fae players have to confess to the fact that their characters are not really people so much as ideas that are assessed with trolling or an acting on this or that impulse if unnaturally complete compared to a human. But even that doesn't ultimately matter! because they could literally change and will be just as true as what they did before because they are a hungering lie.<br /> <br /> So tying Lunars to a sort of animal behavior- well more the sense that man cannot Escape his connection to savagery or escaping being brought down and all of the height of his rationality by something he doesn't choose or necessarily think... That's important., no matter what Humanity does it will always be animals.<br /> well that and will always die<br /> And sneeze<br /> And Hiccup<br /> And be ignorant and dumb and make mistakes<br /> <br /> In some ways the Lunars are tragic because they've been given too much power so they have no room to succeed but no reason to either<br /> <br /> No I don't think there's an actual point to this post just responding to what you wrote<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","user":"Darmani","date":". 05-21-2017, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1498-darmani","name":"Darmani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1498_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T17:09:34-07:00","id":1100268,"title":"","content":"In the &quot;Ask the Devs&quot; thread, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar226_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"226\" data-vbnamecard=\"226\">BrilliantRain</a> expressed curiosity about how Rage could be reflected in all nine Attributes, as Robert Vance said it could.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wits is the Attribute of Resolve and Join Battle. Rage can be used as a shield against persuasion and fear, and also to lower one's brain into the hyper-reactionary &quot;flight or fight&quot; mode.<br /> <br /> Appearance can be used for intimidating Threaten actions when it measures ugliness rather than beauty, and Rage can make you terrifying to behold. On the other hand, we've heard the expression &quot;you're beautiful when you're mad&quot;, and a Lunar's allies might take inspiration for battle in which she leads as a furious goddess of sex and violence.<br /> <br /> Seeing red can narrow your Perception to the point of blindness, but only regarding everything except the one you want to kill. Your focus on them is heightened.<br /> <br /> Charisma is excellent for infecting others with your Rage, or for leveraging your Rage to intimidate.<br /> <br /> Manipulation might use smaller, colder Rages as fuel for delivering the most infuriating of cutting remarks, or for hiding your other feelings behind a mask of anger.<br /> <br /> Dexterity could use your Rage to drive your rush actions, attacks, and counterattacks.<br /> <br /> Rage easily lends itself to feats of strength and destruction.<br /> <br /> Stamina was the source of Relentless Lunar Fury, and their healing and injury-survival powers likely improve when they see red.<br /> <br /> Intelligence... well, I suppose you can better devise and create things that you can use to kill someone you hate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T20:21:50-07:00","id":1100313,"title":"","content":"I feel like <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TranquilFury\" target=\"_blank\">Tranquil Fury</a> is probably a useful trope here. The sort of icy, focusing rage should go pretty well with most of the mental attributes, honestly. And quite possibly many of the other ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T21:32:56-07:00","id":1100336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1092231-lunar-rage?p=1100313#post1100313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/TranquilFury\" target=\"_blank\">Tranquil Fury</a> is probably a useful trope here. The sort of icy, focusing rage should go pretty well with most of the mental attributes, honestly. And quite possibly many of the other ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always thought that was what Relentless Lunar Fury and Battle Fury Focus WERE, to be honest. A laser-precision focus on a specific goal (such as inflicting violence), but without the blood-red haze of a full berserker rage.<br /> <br /> Tranquil Fury is generally the advanced trick rather than the basic one, but that's because it offers better control rather than more power.<br /> <br /> John Wick spends pretty much all of his combat scenes in Battle Fury Focus because he's just that committed to killing anyone who gets in his way, without necessarily killing everyone he sees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T10:19:31-07:00","id":1100490,"title":"","content":"Yeah, John Wick is definitely heavily invested in Resistance. He's that &quot;gritty&quot; sort of action protagonist who endures more harm than he avoids, and Battle Fury Focus is a good presentation of the first thing anyone says about him, to explain why he is so dangerous:<br /> <br /> &quot;John Wick is a man of focus.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> But how do y'all see Relentless Lunar Fury being different from Battle Fury Focus?<br /> <br /> That is, I imagine that many if not most of you would want the two Charms to be noticeably different from each other, but if they're both supposed to capture &quot;committed to violence but not yet uncontrollably berserk&quot;, I'm not sure what could afford to change.<br /> <br /> If you strip out the mental side to focus on the physical hulking out, then you get something more like Terrible Wolverine Onslaught. Which was conceptually a cool Charm that deserved better execution. A stripped down version would also work as a Stamina Charm, considering its reliance on healing Charms.<br /> <br /> The mental half of Battle Fury Focus would become a Lunar Wits Charm, and borrow as much from &quot;Intimacy of the Hunter and the Prey&quot; as from Relentless Lunar Fury. It could be as much a social Charm as a combat Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T11:00:14-07:00","id":1100889,"title":"","content":"<b>FRENZIED BEAR FORTIFICATION<br /> or TERRIBLE WOLVERINE ONSLAUGHT \u2013 The Lunar reaches inside of himself and releases the conservative limits his body places upon itself. For a time, he gains super-human power at the cost of straining his flesh and bone to the breaking point.</b><br /> <i>\u200b1m, 1wp; Reflexive, Until released; No Keywords; Stamina 3, Essence 1 \u2013 Ox-Body Technique</i><br /> <br /> Until he releases this Charm, he enjoys +1 to his Defense and one automatic success to Join Battle actions, attack actions, damage rolls, feats of strength, movement actions, contested rolls against grapple and rush and disengage actions, and reflexive Resistance actions to resist infection and intoxication.<br /> <br /> At the start of any turn in which he does not intend to make an attack or movement action, the character must roll (Willpower) at a difficulty equal to his wound penalty. If he fails, this Charm ends before he acts.<br /> <br /> At the end of every round in which this Charm was active, the character suffers one level of lethal damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>PAIN-NUMBING PRANA</b><br /> <i>\u2014; Permanent; No Keywords; Stamina 4, Essence 2 \u2013 Frenzied Bear Fortification</i><br /> <br /> While Frenzied Bear Fortification is active, the Lunar reduces wound penalties by (Essence / 2, rounded up).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>WILL OF THE STOIC WARRIOR</b><br /> <i>\u2014; Permanent; No Keywords; Stamina 4, Essence 3 \u2013 Pain-Numbing Prana</i><br /> <br /> The Lunar reduces the difficulty on the Willpower roll to restrain Frenzied Bear Fortification by (Essence / 2, rounded up).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>UNSTOPPABLE JUGGERNAUT INCARNATION</b><br /> <i>3m; Reflexive, Indefinite; No Keywords; Stamina 3, Essence 1 \u2013 Ox-Body Technique</i><br /> <br /> A character uses this Charm to avoid falling unconscious when his Incapacitated health level suffers damage, or to regain consciousness afterwards. This Charm doesn\u2019t mitigate wound penalties and does nothing to keep the Lunar from dying if that damage is lethal or aggravated, but otherwise he may continue to act as normal despite his injury. If the damage to his Incapacitated health level is completely healed, he may cancel this Charm without losing consciousness.<br /> <br /> This Charm may be activated for a cost of zero motes if Fortitude of the Aurochs is already active.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>FORTITUDE OF THE AUROCHS</b><br /> <i>3m; Reflexive, Indefinite; No Keywords; Stamina 4, Essence 2 \u2013 Ox-Body Technique</i><br /> <br /> A character uses this Charm to avoid dying when his Incapacitated health level suffers lethal damage. This Charm doesn\u2019t mitigate wound penalties, and without Unstoppable Juggernaut Incarnation, the Lunar will fall unconscious. Further, any lethal wounds beyond the ones necessary to push him into Incapacitated instead upgrade his existing lethal wounds into aggravated wounds. This Charm will not prevent an aggravated wound in his Incapacitated health level from killing him. If the lethal damage to his Incapacitated health level is completely healed or at least is converted to bashing damage, he may cancel this Charm without dying.<br /> <br /> This Charm may be activated for a cost of zero motes if Unstoppable Juggernaut Incarnation is already active.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>MOONSILVER ABSORPTION</b><br /> <i>5m, 1wp; Reflexive, Indefinite; Stackable; Stamina 5, Essence 3 \u2013 Fortitude of the Aurochs</i><br /> <br /> A character uses this Charm to avoid dying when his Incapacitated health level would have suffered aggravated damage. That wound level and any others not yet applied are delayed; record them and ignore them for as long as the motes remain committed to this Charm. The Lunar cannot release commitment to this Charm until he recovers a number of health levels equal to the damage he delayed; if the damage exceeds his total health levels,<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>INDESTRUCTIBLE RECURSIVE DESIGN \u2013 Lunars are survivors, accustomed to the hardships the world demands of its heroes. Knowing that misfortune is in*evitable, hardy Worldwalkers prepare for the worst. With a few moments\u2019 concentration, the Lunar causes his body to grow redundant physical systems\u2014secondary organs, reinforcing musculature, additional ligaments. As the Lunar\u2019s additional body parts are destroyed, they sublimate back into the Essence that formed them. </b><br /> <i>8m; Simple, Indefinite; No Keywords; Stamina 5, Essence 3 \u2013 Moonsilver Absorption</i><br /> <br /> The character gains (Stamina) additional -1 health levels. These levels persist as long as the Charm remains active, and vanish as soon as damage is marked off in them.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd include Bruise-Relief Method and Halting the Scarlet Flow, but I have no idea if or how they might change for this edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-06-2017, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}